      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14198813/assets/93fc83d79679ca9f2b58729af1e3e87c2a01c19c12bc97670fbff398d63d061d.png)\n\nFind ${lim}_{x\\to \\,2}f(x)$ for the function above.\n\n${lim}_{x\\to \\,2}f(x)=$\n{{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "As $x$ approaches $2,$ the value of $f(x)$ approaches $0.$ Consequently, \n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to \\,2}f(x)=0.\n$$\n\nRemember, it does not matter that the actual value of $f(2)$ is $-2.$ All that matters is that as $x$ approaches $2,$ the function $f(x)$ *looks like* it is getting closer and closer to $0.$",
